# Chandra — Code review routing
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When a PR touches a path on the left, the team on the right is auto-requested
# for review. Branch protection on `main` requires at least one approval, so
# CODEOWNERS effectively gates who can merge what.
#
# IMPORTANT — placeholder handles below. Before merging COORD-01, replace the
# `@intelligenzit/<team>` placeholders with either:
#   (a) Actual GitHub team slugs after creating these teams in the org, or
#   (b) Individual GitHub usernames (e.g. `@maheshwar-handle`).
#
# Team composition (2026-05):
#   AWS         -> Maheshwar
#   LangGraph   -> Siva
#   Frontend    -> Aishani
#   Intern/Docs -> Kshiraja
#   Project     -> Phani (Phanindra Malladi)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Fallback owner for anything not matched below. The project lead reviews
# cross-cutting / unowned changes.
*                                       @intelligenzit/chandra-leads

# LangGraph topology, state, nodes, prompts, briefing composer.
/src/chandra/graphs/                    @intelligenzit/langgraph-team
/src/chandra/briefing/                  @intelligenzit/langgraph-team
/src/chandra/prompts/                   @intelligenzit/langgraph-team
/src/chandra/kras.py                    @intelligenzit/langgraph-team

# AWS-facing code: detectors, client factory, IaC, observability.
/src/chandra/aws/                       @intelligenzit/aws-team
/src/chandra/tools/                     @intelligenzit/aws-team
/src/chandra/observability.py           @intelligenzit/aws-team @intelligenzit/langgraph-team
/iac/                                   @intelligenzit/aws-team
/Dockerfile                             @intelligenzit/aws-team
/docker-compose.yml                     @intelligenzit/aws-team

# Frontend surface — Streamlit (legacy debug) + future FastAPI + Next.js.
/src/chandra/dashboard/                 @intelligenzit/frontend-team
/src/chandra/api/                       @intelligenzit/frontend-team

# Database models + migrations — schema changes require AWS + LangGraph signoff
# because both write/read from these tables.
/src/chandra/db/                        @intelligenzit/aws-team @intelligenzit/langgraph-team

# Evals — owned by LangGraph (recall/precision logic) but AWS reviews any
# Terraform changes inside the synthetic env.
/evals/                                 @intelligenzit/langgraph-team

# Tests — owned by whoever owns the code under test; default to LangGraph for
# cross-cutting test infra.
/tests/                                 @intelligenzit/langgraph-team

# Docs + runbooks — Kshiraja is the docs owner per COORD-03 and COORD-05.
/docs/                                  @intelligenzit/docs
/README.md                              @intelligenzit/chandra-leads
/SECURITY.md                            @intelligenzit/chandra-leads
/LICENSE                                @intelligenzit/chandra-leads

# Repo plumbing — only repo admins can change CI / CODEOWNERS to prevent
# bypassing review by editing the rules themselves.
/.github/                               @intelligenzit/chandra-leads
/CODEOWNERS                             @intelligenzit/chandra-leads
/pyproject.toml                         @intelligenzit/chandra-leads
/Makefile                               @intelligenzit/chandra-leads
